From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 14:53:58 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] windows.storage.applicationdata: ApplicationData needs a
 package identity, settings containers, property sets

- ApplicationData.Current fails with APPMODEL_ERROR_NO_PACKAGE (0x80073d54) for a process that has no
  package identity, as Windows does (the todo_wine marks are removed); a packaged process gets one object
- Version and SetVersionAsync (the handler receives a real ISetVersionRequest), ClearAsync and ClearAllAsync
  (settings and the package state folders), DataChanged and SignalDataChanged, RoamingStorageQuota
- LocalSettings and RoamingSettings are ApplicationDataContainers stored in the registry: Values is an
  observable IPropertySet that keeps boxed simple values, Containers and CreateContainer/DeleteContainer
  manage nested containers
- the IInspectable methods (GetIids, GetRuntimeClassName, GetTrustLevel) return real answers
- the folders need Windows.Storage.StorageFolder and still fail with E_NOTIMPL

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01XZFS4SPPzeH5d2c1MuzqCS

